# Golden meeting transcripts for the pass-2 summarizer eval.
# `input` is the transcript exactly as notula renders it for the summarizer
# ([MM:SS] Speaker: text); `context` repeats the lines individually so the
# faithfulness judge can check every summary claim against the source.
# Case `status-only` deliberately contains NO decisions and NO commitments:
# a summarizer that invents some fails faithfulness — conservatism is the
# property under test, not verbosity.
{"id": "standup-bilingual", "input": "[00:02] Rina: Morning semua, quick standup ya. Kemarin aku selesai integrasi payment webhook, tinggal retry logic.\n[00:14] Dimas: Nice. I finished the export endpoint, but the CSV encoding masih ada bug untuk karakter non-latin.\n[00:29] Rina: Oke. We agreed to move the release from Thursday to next Monday, right? Biar sempat regression test.\n[00:41] Speaker 3: Yes, agreed — Monday. I will prepare the staging environment tonight.\n[00:52] Dimas: Aku akan fix the CSV bug by Friday.\n[01:04] Rina: One thing masih open: apakah kita perlu feature flag untuk payment webhook?\n[01:12] Speaker 3: Let's park that, belum urgent.", "context": ["Rina finished the payment webhook integration; retry logic remains.", "Dimas finished the export endpoint but the CSV encoding has a bug with non-latin characters.", "The team agreed to move the release from Thursday to next Monday to allow regression testing.", "Speaker 3 will prepare the staging environment tonight.", "Dimas will fix the CSV bug by Friday.", "Whether a feature flag is needed for the payment webhook is still an open question."], "tags": ["bilingual", "standup"]}
{"id": "sprint-planning", "input": "[00:03] Ayu: Let's size the search revamp. I think the indexing work alone is eight points.\n[00:15] Bagus: Eight is too high. The mapping already exists, five at most.\n[00:31] Ayu: The reindex job still needs a backfill path though.\n[00:44] Bagus: Fine, six, and we split the backfill into its own ticket.\n[00:55] Ayu: Deal — six points, backfill separate. I will write the backfill ticket after this call.\n[01:10] Citra: Who owns the query-parser cleanup? It has been unassigned for two sprints.\n[01:22] Ayu: Good question, let's raise it in retro.", "context": ["Ayu proposed eight points for the indexing work; Bagus argued five.", "They settled on six points with the backfill split into its own ticket.", "Ayu will write the backfill ticket after the call.", "Ownership of the query-parser cleanup is unresolved and will be raised in retro."], "tags": ["planning"]}
{"id": "status-only", "input": "[00:05] Speaker 1: Quick sync — the migration ran overnight without errors.\n[00:16] Speaker 2: Good. Dashboard latency is back to normal after the cache fix last week.\n[00:28] Speaker 1: Support volume is flat, nothing unusual in the queue.\n[00:39] Speaker 2: Same on my side. Nothing else from me.\n[00:44] Speaker 1: Alright, short one today.", "context": ["The migration ran overnight without errors.", "Dashboard latency is back to normal after last week's cache fix.", "Support volume is flat.", "Nothing was decided and no work was assigned in this meeting."], "tags": ["conservatism", "no-decisions"]}
{"id": "vendor-call-id", "input": "[00:04] Putri: Selamat siang Pak, terima kasih sudah menyempatkan waktu.\n[00:12] Hendra: Siang Bu Putri. Jadi terkait kontrak maintenance, kami usulkan perpanjangan dua belas bulan.\n[00:27] Putri: Kami setuju perpanjang dua belas bulan, dengan catatan SLA response time turun dari delapan jam ke empat jam.\n[00:43] Hendra: Empat jam bisa, tapi ada penyesuaian biaya sekitar lima persen.\n[00:55] Putri: Baik, saya akan kirim draf revisi kontrak hari Kamis.\n[01:08] Hendra: [inaudible]\n[01:15] Putri: Maaf Pak, tadi suaranya putus-putus. Bisa diulang via email saja ya.", "context": ["Putri and Hendra discussed extending a maintenance contract.", "They agreed to a twelve-month extension with SLA response time reduced from eight hours to four hours.", "Hendra said the four-hour SLA carries roughly a five percent cost adjustment.", "Putri will send the revised contract draft on Thursday.", "One passage was inaudible and Putri asked for it to be repeated by email."], "tags": ["indonesian", "negotiation"]}
{"id": "incident-review", "input": "[00:02] Farhan: Post-mortem for Tuesday's outage. Timeline first: alerts fired at 09:41, rollback finished 10:07.\n[00:18] Sari: Root cause was the connection pool exhaustion after the ORM upgrade, not the load balancer like we first thought.\n[00:34] Farhan: Right. So the earlier theory is dead. Two follow-ups: we will add a pool saturation alert, and Sari will write the runbook entry.\n[00:52] Sari: Yes, runbook by end of week. Should we also pin the ORM minor version?\n[01:05] Farhan: Undecided — depends on how upstream handles the regression. Let's revisit next week.", "context": ["Alerts fired at 09:41 and rollback finished at 10:07 during Tuesday's outage.", "Root cause was connection pool exhaustion after the ORM upgrade, not the load balancer.", "A pool saturation alert will be added.", "Sari will write the runbook entry by end of week.", "Whether to pin the ORM minor version is undecided and will be revisited next week."], "tags": ["incident"]}
